How ag-psd.mjs was produced (no bundler run here; the upstream bundle is used unchanged):
  npm pack ag-psd@34.1.0 && tar xzf ag-psd-34.1.0.tgz
  { printf '<header>\nconst module = { exports: {} }; const exports = module.exports;\n'
    cat package/dist/bundle.js
    printf '\nconst agPsd = module.exports;\nexport default agPsd;\nexport const { readPsd, writePsd, writePsdBuffer, writePsdUint8Array, initializeCanvas } = agPsd;\n'
  } > ag-psd.mjs
The UMD wrapper sees `module` and `exports` and assigns its exports there, so the file loads as an
ES module in browsers and in node with no build step. Result sha256
f8d611b3b553ce9444418d85ed47cd2418cdfd7a70524033566f67f273ef061a.

